For the cash account (a UK deposit account), the money is held within a client money account. Cash will be held in one or more client money bank account(s) with external account providers of our choice. These account providers can change at any time. This means the Trustee is normally entitled to claim up to £85,000 on behalf of each client for each of these account providers. This limit will also take into account any other accounts you hold with these account providers. We'll hold your cash upon receipt in a client money bank account in line with the Financial Conduct Authority client money rules. Go to aviva.co.uk/bank-interest-rates if you want current details about these account providers.

