uishes its CIP approach from investment pathways and single multi-asset funds, but the actual recommended funds appear as a pair of named vehicles, not explicitly as a CIP portfolio, creating ambiguity about whether the rationale for CIP benefits applies to the actual recommendation. Fifth, the rationale linking 'simplicity' to investment choice is circular: the report says the client wants simplicity and the CIP provides active oversight (more complex), yet does not explain why active oversight serves the simplicity objective better than an alternative. The investment strategy rationale is partly supported (risk alignment, diversification, cost efficiency are present in evidence) but the provider justification contains a cost claim contradicted by evidence, and the alternatives-considered element is not explicitly demonstrated in client-facing terms.","citations":[{"passageId":"P10","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["New solution","Aviva Life & Pensions UK Limited - Pension Portfolio - Choice Platform: Aviva Platform","0.6%","£3,430"]},{"passageId":"P10","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Retained","Zurich - Zurich pension","0.29%","£120,000"]},{"passageId":"P4","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":"CT Universal MAP Balanced Fund C Acc (GBP) | Columbia Threadneedle Fund Management Limited | 50.00; HSBC Global Strategy Balanced Portfolio Accumulation C (GBP) | HSBC Asset Management (Fund Services UK) Limited | 50.00","cells":null},{"passageId":"P12","source":"SIPP research report.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Sort settings","1. Ongoing Charges, ASC 2. 3 Yr Cum. Return, DESC 3. 5 Yr Cum. Return, DESC 4. 5 Yr Ann. Return, DESC"]},{"passageId":"P1","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"The CIP aligns with your long-term goals and offers a more robust and flexible framework compared to a single multiasset fund. It p